generation.text:
31 CFR § 1020.310(g)(1)(i) 

This section requires a mutual fund to have a written anti-money laundering (AML) program approved by its board of directors. The program must include the following minimum elements:

- A system of internal controls to ensure ongoing compliance with the Bank Secrecy Act (BSA) and its implementing regulations;
- Independent testing of the program to ensure its effectiveness;
- Ongoing employee training on the program and the BSA;
- A process for reviewing and updating the program as necessary; and
- A process for filing Suspicious Activity Reports (SARs) and other required reports with the Financial Crimes Enforcement Network (FinCEN).

